/*!
\mainpage Home

Welcome to the manual of the Virtual Experimentation Framework software suite!

New to the VEF?
---------------
- \ref page_gettingstarted describes the installation of the VEF software.
- \ref guided_tour gives a step-by-step tour of some typical use cases where the VEF is applied.

Ready to run your own VEF simulations?
---------------
- \ref user_reference presents the main components of the VEF and discusses 
  how to operate them. 
  The User Reference covers:
  - \ref page_expert_mode that provides a complete control over all the knobs  in the VEF software, 
  - \ref page_simple_mode that helps to carry out standard tasks with minimal
    effort, while sticking to pre-defined defaults, and
  - \ref page_utilities that facilitate a more integral use of the VEF.
- \ref page_theory introduces the foundations of the VEF software and multi-scale crystal
  plasticity models it utilizes.

Need a helping hand?
--------------- 
- \ref page_tutorials 
- \ref examples summarizes the collection of sample problems bundled with the VEF.
- \ref support

